 "finish_summary": "Explored three RTL variants for the 32-bit unsigned comparator: (1) the original spec using Verilog's `<` operator, (2) an explicit balanced log-depth comparator tree built from bitwise lt/eq signals combined hierarchically, and (3) a subtraction-based comparator using a 33-bit subtractor's borrow bit. All three are functionally equivalent. Post-route results showed the original `<`-based RTL achieved the best score (268.926 um\u00b2, WNS 7.62112 ns, score 75.942274), while the balanced tree (271.054 um\u00b2, WNS 7.59353 ns, score 75.664) and subtraction-based (270.788 um\u00b2, WNS 7.60062 ns, score 75.735) variants were both slightly worse in both area and timing. This indicates Yosys/ABC's technology mapping for Nangate45 already produces a near-optimal comparator structure from the native `<` operator, and manual restructuring did not help. The verified best result (baseline RTL, score 75.942274) is retained as the final answer.",
